+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+The tool registry is the single validation boundary between model-produced tool input and consumer executors.
+
+## Execution contract
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's JSON Schema before invoking its executor. Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` that identifies the failing property path and constraint without including property values, and the executor is not invoked. ([validated by: validates tool input while preserving valid and unknown-tool behavior](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L21))
+
+Schema-valid input, including properties the schema does not list, reaches the executor exactly once and unchanged. An unregistered tool name remains the distinct programmer error `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: validates tool input while preserving valid and unknown-tool behavior](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L21))
+
+## Schema lifecycle
+
+A static definition's schema is compiled during registration and reused for execution, so an invalid schema throws an error naming the tool at registration time. A function-valued definition is resolved for every call and that call is validated against its current schema, with compiled validators cached by resolved schema-object identity. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and validates dynamic definitions from each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L59))
+
+## Conversation recovery
+
+A schema rejection is returned to the model as a tool result rather than thrown out of the conversation, allowing the model to correct the call within the orchestrator's bounded tool rounds. ([validated by: returns validation feedback to the model so it can correct a malformed tool call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98))
